            <ArticleTitle>[Headache following intrathecal therapy in acute leukemia: trial of tiapride as a symptomatic treatment (author's transl)].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>993-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>11 patients experienced 40 intrathecal injections of cytotoxic drugs during the treatment of acute leukemia. Tiapride was used as a preventive or curative therapy for headache. Results were found excellent or good in 70% of cases. Frequency and intensity of headache were reduced by half. Tiapride seems more effective in early headache than in cephalalgia occuring later.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
